## Known Bugs to Fix
- All previously listed bugs have been resolved.
- `consent.tsx`: `useI18n()` hook outside component → fixed (uses `I18n` directly, no hook needed).
- `config/difficultyConfig.ts`: bad import → fixed (no I18n import needed; function returns labels directly).
- All 6 game files: `router.back()` on exit → replaced with `router.replace('/(tabs)/explore')` throughout.

## Architecture Notes

### Navigation
- Tab Router: `app/(tabs)/index.tsx` (Home), `app/(tabs)/explore.tsx` (Games), `app/(tabs)/activity.tsx` (Stats)
- Game screens: `app/game/*.tsx`
- Always use `router.replace('/(tabs)/explore')` on game exit — never `router.back()` (causes blank screen on web)

### Localization
- `services/i18n.ts` → `I18n.t('key')` or hook: `const { t } = useI18n()`
- All keys must exist in `locales/en.json` and all 14 other locale files
- When adding new keys, add to all 15 locales: ar, de, en, es, fa, fi, fr, hi, it, ja, ko, nl, pt-BR, tr, zh

### Cognitive Profile & Scoring
- `services/engine/AnalysisEngine.ts` → EWMA alpha=0.05 (kept low to reduce volatility)
- `services/storage.ts` → AsyncStorage wrapper
- `services/progression.ts` → XP, level, tier system

## App Store Context
- App is being prepared for App Store submission. Framing must be "scientific, not medical".
- Tone: "Mentra is a gym for your brain, not a hospital." — maintain this throughout.
- Always run `npx tsc --noEmit` before committing any new feature.
- Web testing: `npx expo start --web --port 8083`

